-- title:
--   Integral modular unit on Γ_H(q²M') vanishing at ∞
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number, and let $N=q^2M'$. Write $H=$ [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) for the kernel of the reduction map $(\mathbb Z/N)^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, and let $\Gamma_H$ be [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $SL(2,\mathbb Z)$ of the set of $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N)$ whose lower-right entry, taken as a unit of $\mathbb Z/N$ via [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121), lies in $H$; it is regarded as a subgroup of $GL(2,\mathbb R)$. The assertion is that there exist a weight $k\in\mathbb Z$, modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H$, and power series $p_f,p_g,h\in\mathbb Z[[X]]$ such that $p_f$ and $p_g$ map under $\mathbb Z\to\mathbb C$ to the width-one $\mathsf q$-expansions of $f$ and of $g$ respectively, $p_g\neq 0$, $p_f=p_g\,h$, the constant coefficient of $h$ vanishes, and the Laurent series over $\mathbb Q$ obtained from $h$ by [`ModularCurve.intSeriesC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L69) is integral over the image of the ring homomorphism $\mathbb Z[X]\to\mathbb Q((\mathsf q))$ sending $X$ to $(\mathrm{ModularCurve.jq})^{-1}$, i.e. it satisfies a monic polynomial with coefficients in $\mathbb Z[1/j]$, where [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) is $\mathsf q^{-1}$ times the integral power series `jNum` read over $\mathbb Q$; and, in addition, for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(N)$ there are modular forms $f_1,g_1$ of the same weight $k$ on $\Gamma_H$, power series $p_{f_1},p_{g_1},h_1\in\mathbb Z[[X]]$ and a nonzero $c\in\mathbb C$ with: $p_{f_1},p_{g_1}$ integral $\mathsf q$-expansions of $f_1,g_1$ in the same sense, $f_1=c\,(f\mid_k\gamma)$ and $g_1=c\,(g\mid_k\gamma)$ as functions on the upper half-plane, $p_{g_1}\neq0$, $p_{f_1}=p_{g_1}h_1$, and, provided the unit [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units N γ`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) does not belong to the subgroup generated by $H$ together with $-1\in(\mathbb Z/N)^\times$, the constant coefficient of $h_1$ is a unit of $\mathbb Z$.
--
--   This packages the Siegel-unit construction: the ratio $f/g$ is a modular unit on $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$ whose expansion vanishes at $\infty$, is integral over $\mathbb Z[1/j]$, and has unit constant term at each translate $\gamma\infty$ with $d(\gamma)\not\equiv\pm1 \bmod q$. It is used by the three [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_mem_chartAlgInf_coeff_zero_eq_zero_forall_algEquiv_coeff_zero_ne_xH`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_mem_chartAlgInf_coeff_zero_eq_zero_forall_algEquiv_coeff_zero_ne_xH) statements, which separate the cusp $\infty$ from its nontrivial diamond translates in the full-level construction.
